  "title": "Cross-Model Attribute Selection and Answer-Conditioned Chain-of-Thought Distillation for Industrial Vision with Small VLMs",
  "summary": "Both reports highlight the importance of attribute selection in vision-language models (VLMs) by emphasizing the need to avoid class names and use image-based attributes to improve interpretable zero-shot classification. They both focus on distribution shift and demonstrate how attribute prompts can be effectively selected by leveraging image data. Additionally, both studies focus on improving tool choice and user alignment through memory conditioning.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Fact 1: Both reports emphasize the need to avoid class names and use image-based attributes in VLMs to improve interpretable zero-shot classification.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fact 2: Both studies demonstrate the effectiveness of attribute prompts and memory conditioning in enhancing tool choice and user alignment.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fact 3: Both reports highlight the importance of leveraging image data to address distribution shift and improve model performance.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
